and then, after the loop, add 1 to yield the proper final result. (A little algebra shows that with these changes the “sequence” will be 1, 2, 3, … so that after n–2 iterations the final answer is (n–2)+1 = n–1 and adding one more returns n.) With n = 5 the loop runs three times so that:  

